## Phase 18 ConsumerRunningInfo Fastjson raw decoder continuation

- Recorded: 2026-10-24 02:23:37 UTC
- Code revision: `9180556a2f694b43ffc2ecd0417b6f51430ccf5e`
- Fixture: `fixtures/consumer/running-info.json`, SHA-256
  `495f040623c010c13a4d70f004db4d0529bd8fcda93530671015c69cb49f1e06`

The pinned Java `RemotingSerializable.decode(byte[], ConsumerRunningInfo.class)`
calls Fastjson `parseObject`. Rust's typed decoder first converted special
object-valued `MessageQueue` map keys but did not normalize Fastjson input.
Four invoked cases now cover trailing text and a second document after raw
U+001A, a raw marker inside a string, and single-quoted input with a trailing
comma. Rust matches Java acceptance and encoded fields; a populated Java body
also round-trips through the typed decoder. Set-valued fields are compared
without imposing iteration order.

